# SLA Clock

## Summary
One ref-counted interval for the whole page. Badges and lens predicates subscribe to the same ticking instant, so a queue of fifty rows costs one timer and the rail's count never disagrees with a row's badge.

## API
`slaClock.now` (tracked); `slaClock.subscribe()` / `slaClock.unsubscribe()` are a ref-counted pair — the interval exists only while at least one subscriber is registered.

## Usage
```ts
import { slaClock } from '@cardstack/catalog/cards/service-desk/utils/sla-clock';

constructor(owner: unknown, args: Args) {
  super(owner, args);
  slaClock.subscribe();
  registerDestructor(this, () => slaClock.unsubscribe());
}
get now() { return slaClock.now; }
```

## Non-goals
Not a scheduler; it only reports the current instant once a second.
